# Faction_Design — Skeleton

## 1. Applies when
Games with multiple playable/hostile factions (open_world_rpg, strategy_simulation).

## 2. This document owns
- Faction mechanical identity: available units/buildings/abilities per faction.
- Faction relationship matrix (ally/hostile/neutral) and reputation rules.
- Asymmetry budgets (what each faction trades off).

## 3. This document does NOT own
- Faction lore, history and motivation — Narrative_Bible.
- Campaign mission content — Mission / Quest.
- Individual unit stats — Unit / Enemy design.

## 4. Recommended chapter structure
1. Faction roster / 2. Identity & fantasy / 3. Relationship matrix / 4. Reputation system / 5. Asymmetry budget / 6. Mechanical kits / 7. Open questions

## 5. Common boundaries
- Faction vs Bible: mechanics here, narrative truth in the Bible; both reference the same faction IDs.
- Relationship changes are data (matrix updates), not prose retcons.

## 6. Common audit rules
- Relationship matrix is symmetric-consistent (A→B matches B→A semantics).
- Every faction in the Bible has a row here (or is explicitly non-mechanical).
